The license above covers the source in this repository and nothing else.

BlockyEngine is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Mojang
Studios or Microsoft. "Minecraft" is a trademark of Mojang Studios.

The engine ships no game assets and requires none: block textures are
generated in code, characters are drawn in code, and the built-in font is its
own. What it can do is *read* an installation you already have -- a client
`.jar` or a resource pack -- and some of the images in `docs/gallery/` were
rendered that way. Those images show textures belonging to their respective
owners, are included to demonstrate the reader rather than to redistribute the
artwork, and are marked as such in the gallery. Nothing under `engine/`,
`game/` or `scenes/` contains any of it.
